From 570a6cfe97ab1e0ea6827ba4ce841a79681c0543 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.xyz>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 19:14:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] aarch64: start secondary CPUs on the Raspberry Pi 3

The Raspberry Pi firmware parks secondary cores in a spin-table loop and
the BCM2836 local interrupt controller has no GIC, so SMP needs:

- spin-table enable method: parse cpu-release-addr, release the core by
  writing a trampoline entry to it, and pass the BootArgs address through
  a slot in the trampoline page, since spin-table passes no context.
- BCM2836 IPIs through the per-core mailbox 0, reported like GIC SGI IDs.
- Per-core routing of all four architected timer interrupts. Before, only
  the non-secure physical timer could be enabled, not the virtual timer
  the kernel uses on Cortex-A53.

Tested in QEMU raspi3b: all four CPUs pass the IPI/timer self-test and
come online, the system boots to the login prompt.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
